# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-24
#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: description
#, no-wrap
msgid "Learn which time-based usage fields in the IBM Quantum Compute API to disregard, and which resource unit (RU) fields replace them."
msgstr "Découvre quels champs d'utilisation basés sur le temps de l'API IBM Quantum Compute tu dois ignorer, et quels champs en unités de ressources (RU) les remplacent."

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-24
#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#, no-wrap
msgid "Migrate to resource units (RUs) in the IBM Quantum Compute API"
msgstr "Migrer vers les unités de ressources (RU) dans l'API IBM Quantum Compute"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-24
#. type: Title #
#, no-wrap
msgid "Migrate to resource units (RUs) in the IBM Quantum Compute API {#migrate-to-resource-units-rus-in-the-ibm-quantum-compute-api}"
msgstr "Migrer vers les unités de ressources (RU) dans l'API IBM Quantum Compute {#migrate-to-resource-units-rus-in-the-ibm-quantum-compute-api}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-24
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "IBM Quantum&reg; Platform now measures usage in resource units (RUs). An RU is the unit that IBM Quantum uses to measure and bill the usage of all workloads. Before this change, the platform measured usage as QPU time in seconds or milliseconds. For more information about RUs, see [Resource units](/guides/plans-overview#resource-units).\n"
msgstr "IBM Quantum&reg; Platform mesure désormais l'utilisation en unités de ressources (RU). Une RU est l'unité qu'IBM Quantum utilise pour mesurer et facturer l'utilisation de toutes les charges de travail. Avant ce changement, la plateforme mesurait l'utilisation sous forme de temps QPU en secondes ou en millisecondes. Pour plus d'informations sur les RU, consulte [Unités de ressources](/guides/plans-overview#resource-units).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-24
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Today, the API returns two sets of fields: the old time fields and the new RU fields. Your integration continues to work. In a future release, IBM Quantum will remove the time fields. Change your integration to read the RU fields now.\n"
msgstr "Aujourd'hui, l'API renvoie deux ensembles de champs : les anciens champs de temps et les nouveaux champs RU. Ton intégration continue de fonctionner. Dans une prochaine version, IBM Quantum supprimera les champs de temps. Modifie dès maintenant ton intégration pour lire les champs RU.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-24
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This guide uses these terms:\n"
msgstr "Ce guide utilise les termes suivants :\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-24
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Workload**: A job, a session, a batch, or a function run.\n"
msgstr "**Charge de travail** : un job, une session, un batch ou une exécution de fonction.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-24
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**QPU workload**: A job, a session, or a batch. A QPU workload runs only on a QPU.\n"
msgstr "**Charge de travail QPU** : un job, une session ou un batch. Une charge de travail QPU s'exécute uniquement sur un QPU.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-24
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Function workload**: A function run. A function workload can use classical compute and an execution license, and it can also use a QPU.\n"
msgstr "**Charge de travail de fonction** : une exécution de fonction. Une charge de travail de fonction peut utiliser du calcul classique et une licence d'exécution, et elle peut aussi utiliser un QPU.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-24
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Session**: A group of jobs that run together on one QPU.\n"
msgstr "**Session** : un groupe de jobs qui s'exécutent ensemble sur un même QPU.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-24
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Instance**: A service instance. It owns workloads and has usage limits.\n"
msgstr "**Instance** : une instance de service. Elle possède des charges de travail et a des limites d'utilisation.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-24
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Plan**: The service plan of an account. It sets the usage limits for all instances in the account.\n"
msgstr "**Plan** : le plan de service d'un compte. Il définit les limites d'utilisation de toutes les instances du compte.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-24
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"  This guide uses version 0.57.2 of the [OpenAPI spec](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/api/openapi.json).\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"  Ce guide utilise la version 0.57.2 de la [spécification OpenAPI](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/api/openapi.json).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-24
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  The `IBM-API-Version` header value must be `2026-04-15` or a later supported API version.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"  La valeur de l'en-tête `IBM-API-Version` doit être `2026-04-15` ou une version ultérieure de l'API prise en charge.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-24
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Summary {#summary}"
msgstr "Résumé {#summary}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-24
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Endpoint | Disregard | Read instead |\n"
"| --- | --- | --- |\n"
"| `GET /v1/jobs`, `GET /v1/jobs/{id}/metrics` | `usage.qpu_charge_time_seconds` | `usage.value` |\n"
"| `GET /v1/workloads` | `workloads[].usage.qpu_charge_time_seconds` | `workloads[].usage.value` |\n"
"| `POST /v1/sessions`, `GET /v1/sessions/{id}` | `elapsed_time` | `usage.value` |\n"
"| `GET /v1/instances/usage` | `usage_consumed_seconds`, `usage_limit_seconds`, `usage_allocation_seconds` | `usage_consumed_ru`, `usage_limit_ru`, `usage_allocation_ru` |\n"
"| `GET /v1/accounts/{id}` | `plans[].usage_limit_seconds`, `plans[].usage_allocation_seconds`, `plans[].unallocated_usage_seconds` | `plans[].usage_limit_ru`, `plans[].usage_allocation_ru`, `plans[].unallocated_usage_ru` |\n"
"| Resource Controller API: Create, update, and read service instances | `instance_limit_seconds`, `usage_allocation_seconds` | `instance_limit_ru`, `usage_allocation_ru` |\n"
"| `GET /v1/analytics/usage`, `GET /v1/analytics/usage_grouped`, `GET /v1/analytics/usage_grouped_by_date` | Each usage field in milliseconds | The matching field with the `_ru` suffix |\n"
msgstr ""
"| Point de terminaison | À ignorer | À lire à la place |\n"
"| --- | --- | --- |\n"
"| `GET /v1/jobs`, `GET /v1/jobs/{id}/metrics` | `usage.qpu_charge_time_seconds` | `usage.value` |\n"
"| `GET /v1/workloads` | `workloads[].usage.qpu_charge_time_seconds` | `workloads[].usage.value` |\n"
"| `POST /v1/sessions`, `GET /v1/sessions/{id}` | `elapsed_time` | `usage.value` |\n"
"| `GET /v1/instances/usage` | `usage_consumed_seconds`, `usage_limit_seconds`, `usage_allocation_seconds` | `usage_consumed_ru`, `usage_limit_ru`, `usage_allocation_ru` |\n"
"| `GET /v1/accounts/{id}` | `plans[].usage_limit_seconds`, `plans[].usage_allocation_seconds`, `plans[].unallocated_usage_seconds` | `plans[].usage_limit_ru`, `plans[].usage_allocation_ru`, `plans[].unallocated_usage_ru` |\n"
"| API Resource Controller : créer, mettre à jour et lire des instances de service | `instance_limit_seconds`, `usage_allocation_seconds` | `instance_limit_ru`, `usage_allocation_ru` |\n"
"| `GET /v1/analytics/usage`, `GET /v1/analytics/usage_grouped`, `GET /v1/analytics/usage_grouped_by_date` | Chaque champ d'utilisation en millisecondes | Le champ correspondant avec le suffixe `_ru` |\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-24
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The sections that follow give the details for each endpoint.\n"
msgstr "Les sections suivantes donnent les détails pour chaque point de terminaison.\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Jobs {#jobs}"
msgstr "Jobs {#jobs}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-24
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Endpoints: `GET /v1/jobs` and `GET /v1/jobs/{id}/metrics`.\n"
msgstr "Points de terminaison : `GET /v1/jobs` et `GET /v1/jobs/{id}/metrics`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-24
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Disregard | Read instead |\n"
"| --- | --- |\n"
"| `usage.qpu_charge_time_seconds` | `usage.value` |\n"
msgstr ""
"| À ignorer | À lire à la place |\n"
"| --- | --- |\n"
"| `usage.qpu_charge_time_seconds` | `usage.value` |\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-24
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The `usage` object also has these fields:\n"
msgstr "L'objet `usage` contient aussi les champs suivants :\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-24
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`usage.unit`: The unit of `usage.value`. The value is always `\"resource_units\"`.\n"
msgstr "`usage.unit` : l'unité de `usage.value`. La valeur est toujours `\"resource_units\"`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-24
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`usage.status`: The billing status. The value is `\"pending\"` or `\"complete\"`. If the status is `\"pending\"`, the platform can still change the value. Do not use a pending value as the final usage.\n"
msgstr "`usage.status` : le statut de facturation. La valeur est `\"pending\"` ou `\"complete\"`. Si le statut est `\"pending\"`, la plateforme peut encore modifier la valeur. N'utilise pas une valeur en attente comme utilisation finale.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-24
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`usage.details[]`: The usage for each billing metric. The `value` of each entry is in RUs.\n"
msgstr "`usage.details[]` : l'utilisation pour chaque métrique de facturation. La `value` de chaque entrée est en RU.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Example:\n"
msgstr "Example:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-24
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The field `usage.details[].metric.value` is not the usage in RUs. It is the quantity of the metric that the platform used to calculate the RUs. Each metric has its own unit. For example, the unit of a QPU metric is seconds. For the usage, read `usage.details[].value`.\n"
msgstr "Le champ `usage.details[].metric.value` n'est pas l'utilisation en RU. C'est la quantité de la métrique que la plateforme a utilisée pour calculer les RU. Chaque métrique a sa propre unité. Par exemple, l'unité d'une métrique QPU est la seconde. Pour l'utilisation, lis `usage.details[].value`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-24
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Workloads {#workloads}"
msgstr "Charges de travail {#workloads}"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Endpoint: `GET /v1/workloads`.\n"
msgstr "Endpoint: `GET /v1/workloads`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-24
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Each item in `workloads[]` has a `usage` object. This object has the same fields as the `usage` object of a job.\n"
msgstr "Chaque élément de `workloads[]` possède un objet `usage`. Cet objet a les mêmes champs que l'objet `usage` d'un job.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-24
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Disregard | Read instead |\n"
"| --- | --- |\n"
"| `workloads[].usage.qpu_charge_time_seconds` | `workloads[].usage.value` |\n"
msgstr ""
"| À ignorer | À lire à la place |\n"
"| --- | --- |\n"
"| `workloads[].usage.qpu_charge_time_seconds` | `workloads[].usage.value` |\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-24
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "If a workload is still running, `usage` is `null`.\n"
msgstr "Si une charge de travail est encore en cours d'exécution, `usage` vaut `null`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-24
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Function workloads {#function-workloads}"
msgstr "Charges de travail de fonction {#function-workloads}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-24
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The usage of a function workload is in RUs, the same as for a QPU workload. A function workload can use more than one metric:\n"
msgstr "L'utilisation d'une charge de travail de fonction est en RU, comme pour une charge de travail QPU. Une charge de travail de fonction peut utiliser plus d'une métrique :\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-24
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**QPU usage.** This is metered per second of quantum time. See [Execution modes](/guides/execution-modes).\n"
msgstr "**Utilisation du QPU.** Elle est mesurée par seconde de temps quantique. Voir [Modes d'exécution](/guides/execution-modes).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-24
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Classical compute usage.** This is metered per second of [classical time](/guides/managed-workflow-compute-profiles).\n"
msgstr "**Utilisation du calcul classique.** Elle est mesurée par seconde de [temps classique](/guides/managed-workflow-compute-profiles).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-24
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Execution license cost.** This is metered per workload, based on the [size of the problem passed to a function](/guides/functions#overview-of-available-functions).\n"
msgstr "**Coût de la licence d'exécution.** Il est mesuré par charge de travail, en fonction de la [taille du problème transmis à une fonction](/guides/functions#overview-of-available-functions).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-24
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The platform converts the quantity of each metric to RUs. Thus, all usage values are in RUs:\n"
msgstr "La plateforme convertit la quantité de chaque métrique en RU. Ainsi, toutes les valeurs d'utilisation sont en RU :\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-24
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`usage.value` is the usage of the workload, in RUs.\n"
msgstr "`usage.value` est l'utilisation de la charge de travail, en RU.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-24
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`usage.details[].value` is the usage for one metric, in RUs.\n"
msgstr "`usage.details[].value` est l'utilisation pour une métrique, en RU.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-24
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`usage.details[].metric.value` is the quantity of the metric, in the unit of that metric. It is not in RUs.\n"
msgstr "`usage.details[].metric.value` est la quantité de la métrique, dans l'unité de cette métrique. Elle n'est pas en RU.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-24
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "If you show or add usage values, use `usage.value` and `usage.details[].value`. Do not use `usage.details[].metric.value`.\n"
msgstr "Si tu affiches ou additionnes des valeurs d'utilisation, utilise `usage.value` et `usage.details[].value`. N'utilise pas `usage.details[].metric.value`.\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Sessions {#sessions}"
msgstr "Sessions {#sessions}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-24
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Endpoints: `POST /v1/sessions` and `GET /v1/sessions/{id}`.\n"
msgstr "Points de terminaison : `POST /v1/sessions` et `GET /v1/sessions/{id}`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-24
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Disregard | Read instead |\n"
"| --- | --- |\n"
"| `elapsed_time` (seconds) | `usage.value` |\n"
msgstr ""
"| À ignorer | À lire à la place |\n"
"| --- | --- |\n"
"| `elapsed_time` (secondes) | `usage.value` |\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-24
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The session `usage` object has `unit` and `details[]`. These fields work the same as in the job `usage` object, with the exception of the `status` field, which is omitted for sessions.\n"
msgstr "L'objet `usage` d'une session contient `unit` et `details[]`. Ces champs fonctionnent comme dans l'objet `usage` d'un job, à l'exception du champ `status`, qui est omis pour les sessions.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-24
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The fields `interactive_ttl`, `max_ttl`, and `active_ttl` do not change. They are time limits (TTL means \"time to live\"), not usage. Their unit stays seconds.\n"
msgstr "Les champs `interactive_ttl`, `max_ttl` et `active_ttl` ne changent pas. Ce sont des limites de temps (TTL signifie « time to live »), pas de l'utilisation. Leur unité reste la seconde.\n"

