# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-24
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The total in `usage_ru` includes more than the total in `usage`:\n"
msgstr "Le total de `usage_ru` inclut plus que le total de `usage` :\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-24
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`usage` is the sum of QPU time for sessions, individual jobs, and functions.\n"
msgstr "`usage` est la somme du temps QPU des sessions, des jobs individuels et des fonctions.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-24
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`usage_ru` is the sum of usage for sessions, individual jobs, and functions. For functions, it also includes classical compute and license cost.\n"
msgstr "`usage_ru` est la somme de l'utilisation des sessions, des jobs individuels et des fonctions. Pour les fonctions, elle inclut aussi le calcul classique et le coût de la licence.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-24
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Thus, `usage_ru` is not only `usage` in a different unit.\n"
msgstr "Ainsi, `usage_ru` n'est pas simplement `usage` dans une autre unité.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-24
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The fields `queue_time`, `avg_queue_time`, and `max_queue_time` do not change. They measure wait time, not usage. Their unit stays milliseconds.\n"
msgstr "Les champs `queue_time`, `avg_queue_time` et `max_queue_time` ne changent pas. Ils mesurent le temps d'attente, pas l'utilisation. Leur unité reste la milliseconde.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-24
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Fields that do not change {#fields-that-do-not-change}"
msgstr "Champs qui ne changent pas {#fields-that-do-not-change}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-24
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "These fields contain time values, but they do not measure usage. IBM Quantum does not plan to replace them:\n"
msgstr "Ces champs contiennent des valeurs de temps, mais ils ne mesurent pas l'utilisation. IBM Quantum ne prévoit pas de les remplacer :\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-24
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`wait_time_seconds` on backends: The estimated wait in the queue.\n"
msgstr "`wait_time_seconds` sur les backends : l'attente estimée dans la file d'attente.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-24
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`circuits_execution_time_ns` in `GET /v1/jobs/{id}/metrics`: The time that the job ran on the QPU.\n"
msgstr "`circuits_execution_time_ns` dans `GET /v1/jobs/{id}/metrics` : le temps pendant lequel le job s'est exécuté sur le QPU.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-24
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`interactive_ttl`, `max_ttl`, and `active_ttl` on sessions.\n"
msgstr "`interactive_ttl`, `max_ttl` et `active_ttl` sur les sessions.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-24
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`queue_time`, `avg_queue_time`, and `max_queue_time` in analytics.\n"
msgstr "`queue_time`, `avg_queue_time` et `max_queue_time` dans les analyses.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-24
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`rep_times` and `circuit_duration` in backend configuration.\n"
msgstr "`rep_times` et `circuit_duration` dans la configuration du backend.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-24
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Migration steps {#migration-steps}"
msgstr "Étapes de migration {#migration-steps}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-24
#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Find each old field in your code. Search for `qpu_charge_time_seconds`, `elapsed_time`, the `_seconds` fields in this guide, and the analytics fields in milliseconds.\n"
msgstr "Trouve chaque ancien champ dans ton code. Recherche `qpu_charge_time_seconds`, `elapsed_time`, les champs `_seconds` de ce guide et les champs d'analyses en millisecondes.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-24
#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Change each old field to the RU field in the tables of this guide.\n"
msgstr "Remplace chaque ancien champ par le champ RU des tableaux de ce guide.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-24
#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "If you create or update service instances with the Resource Controller API, send `instance_limit_ru` and `usage_allocation_ru`. Do not send the `_seconds` parameters.\n"
msgstr "Si tu crées ou mets à jour des instances de service avec l'API Resource Controller, envoie `instance_limit_ru` et `usage_allocation_ru`. N'envoie pas les paramètres `_seconds`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-24
#. type: Bullet: '4. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Change the labels in your user interface. Show \"RU\" or \"resource units\", not \"seconds\" or \"minutes\". Do not convert RUs to time. There is no fixed rate between RUs and time.\n"
msgstr "Modifie les libellés de ton interface utilisateur. Affiche « RU » ou « unités de ressources », pas « secondes » ou « minutes ». Ne convertis pas les RU en temps. Il n'existe pas de taux fixe entre les RU et le temps.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-24
#. type: Bullet: '5. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "If you read `usage.details[]`, use `value` for the usage in RUs. Do not use `metric.value`, because its unit is the unit of the metric.\n"
msgstr "Si tu lis `usage.details[]`, utilise `value` pour l'utilisation en RU. N'utilise pas `metric.value`, car son unité est celle de la métrique.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-24
#. type: Bullet: '6. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "If `usage.status` is `\"pending\"`, show the value as provisional.\n"
msgstr "Si `usage.status` vaut `\"pending\"`, affiche la valeur comme provisoire.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-24
#. type: Bullet: '7. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "If an RU field is missing or `null`, use the same logic that you use for the old field today.\n"
msgstr "Si un champ RU est absent ou vaut `null`, utilise la même logique que celle que tu utilises aujourd'hui pour l'ancien champ.\n"
